The soundset is great. As I play through the game, I am compiling a list 
of sounds and triggers I wanted to add. Maybe we could collaborate on 
that, because some of the sounds I have I think would fit in well with 
the theme of your soundset being "voiceless."

I also wanted to point out an interesting BUG with Nethack's sound 
system that has been giving me trouble for ages and may have confused 
you as well, regarding the playback of wav files. I finally isolated it, 
and here it is:

If there is more than one text sound trigger on the same output line, 
the one that will be played will be the one that comes FIRST in the 
defaults.nh sound trigger list.

A good example of this is when Elbereth is engraved into the ground. 
Consider the line:

Something here is engraved in the ground. You read: "Elbereth"

Intuitively you would think that the program would first try to play the 
"*You read:*" trigger first, then play the "*Elbereth*" trigger last, so 
you would hear the Elbereth sound last. Alas, this is not the case. The 
only sound you hear for this line is the for the "*You read:*" trigger.

However, when I switched the location of the "*Elbereth*" trigger all 
over the file, I realized that when it played and when it did not was 
entirely dependent on if it was placed BEFORE or AFTER the "*You read:*" 
trigger.

